import ../../helpers/driver.dl

appearance overlay appearance:
    flow is overlay
appearance covered appearance:
    height is 60
    background is UI ink 30 35 40
appearance link appearance:
    padding is 8
appearance card appearance:
    background is UI ink 250 250 249
    padding is 8
appearance text appearance:
    font size is 16

document layers test:
    region "Layers" using overlay appearance:
        paragraph "Behind" using text appearance:
            link "Underneath" to "/under" using text appearance
        region "Cover" using covered appearance:
            link "Top link" to "/top" using link appearance
    region "Card" using card appearance:
        paragraph "Selectable content" using text appearance

set instance to an instance of layers test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 300 by 200 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set point to a UI point at 12.0 and 15.0
require condition ((the UI text hit at point in (the address of view)) = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run)) reporting "Text beneath an opaque control is still hittable"
set top to the UI layout labeled "Top link" in (view's layout)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at 12.0 15.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
set view's seconds to 0.016
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set view's seconds to 0.032
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's hot = top) reporting "Painting discarded the document hover target"
require condition (top's hover > 0.0) reporting "A document link did not animate its hover state"
set paragraph to the UI layout labeled "Selectable content" in (view's layout)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (paragraph's painted bounds' x + 2.0) (paragraph's painted bounds' y + 10.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's selection's caret source = (the address of (paragraph's text source))) reporting "An opaque card blocked selection of its own text"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Document hit testing follows paint order and preserves hover and selection."
